<title>HONG KONG: HK Bank sets up US$2bln MTN programme.</title>
<headline>HK Bank sets up US$2bln MTN programme.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-05-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hongkong Bank, a subsidiary of HSBC Plc, said on Thursday it had established a US$2 billion medium-term note (MTN) programme.</p>
<p>The programme was intended to facilitate its branches' funding requirements in the region in the currencies of Asian and Group of Seven countries -- Britain, Canada, France, Germany, Italy, Japan and the United States -- it said in a statement.</p>
<p>It said the MTN programme would complement its existing certificate of deposit programme by tapping &quot;a different and wider investor base&quot;.</p>
<p>Hongkong Bank said it had applied to list the programme in Hong Kong.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong newsroom (852) 2843 6371</p>
</text>
